{"type":"after","callId":"call@208","endTime":53784.283,"result":{"matches":true,"received":{"value":{"s":"A close-up inside Science lab with fixed handrails, labeled work equipment, two cabin directions, a floating object, and the astronaut. The flight-deck side leads to Flight deck. The engineering side leads to Medical bay. The current compartment is the selected destination. Cabin condition: Station maneuver. Payload: Hands free. A loose sample keeps moving until a hand, rail, or wall stops it. Work result: only the Rail 04 handhold controls the body, allowing the astronaut to pivot while the specimen bag remains in motion."},"ariaSnapshot":"- main \"Mission briefing for Mars\":\n  - navigation \"Mission progress\":\n    - text: Mission progress Step 2 of 5\n    - list:\n      - listitem: Destination\n      - listitem: Briefing\n      - listitem: Power\n      - listitem: Decision\n      - listitem: Review\n  - img \"View of Mars from approach trajectory\"\n  - heading \"🔴 Mission to Mars\" [level=4]\n  - paragraph: The Red Planet — our closest neighbor.\n  - text: \"Gravity: 3.72 m/s² Temp: -60°C avg Atmosphere: CO₂ (95%), thin Travel: 210 days ⚠️ dust storms ⚠️ radiation ⚠️ thin atmosphere ⚠️ cold 📂 Mission Dossier Risk: training\"\n  - paragraph: Can the crew survive Mars while turning dust storms into evidence about geology?\n  - text: Arrival\n  - paragraph: Confirm orbit, comms, and immediate dust storms controls.\n  - text: Survey\n  - paragraph: Collect evidence for geology while protecting O2 and hull margins.\n  - text: Departure\n  - paragraph: Prioritize samples, return trajectory, and what evidence is strong enough to bring home.\n  - text: geology\n  - paragraph: What does geology reveal about Mars?\n  - text: astrobiology\n  - paragraph: What does astrobiology reveal about Mars?\n  - text: atmospheric science\n  - paragraph: What does atmospheric science reveal about Mars?\n  - region \"Float through the mission cabin\":\n    - text: Optional practice • launch remains available\n    - heading \"Float through the mission cabin\" [level=2]\n    - paragraph: Choose a compartment, compare movement methods, then select a restraint setup for its activity. In microgravity, weightlessness removes foot friction — not mass or inertia.\n    - button \"Skip practice · Continue to power setup\"\n    - list \"Cabin readiness requirements\":\n      - text: Readiness checklist\n      - listitem: 0 of 2 activities\n      - listitem: 1 of 2 controlled moves\n      - text: 1 maneuver-safe 1 work correction\n    - text: Cabin visual\n    - group \"Cabin visual view\":\n      - button \"Route map\"\n      - button \"Inside view\" [pressed]\n    - img \"Science lab interior close-up\": FLIGHT MED RACK LAB-2 RAIL 04 LAB MANEUVER\n    - text: \"Current:\"\n    - strong: Science lab\n    - text: \"Final goal:\"\n    - strong: Science lab\n    - text: \"Payload:\"\n    - strong: ○ Hands free • 0 kg • 1.00× inertia\n    - text: \"Condition:\"\n    - strong: 🛰️ Station maneuver\n    - text: 1 fixed point (Rail 04 handhold) → body pivots; specimen bag drifts.\n    - heading \"1. Choose a final compartment\" [level=3]\n    - group \"Interior destination\":\n      - button \"🧭 Flight deck Confirm the attitude reference and secure the command tablet.\"\n      - button \"🧪 Science lab Tether the specimen bag before opening the experiment rack.\" [pressed]\n      - button \"🩺 Medical bay Stow the medical kit and brace the patient restraint.\"\n      - button \"⚙️ Engineering Inspect the oxygen scrubber and lock the tool pouch.\"\n    - heading \"2. Set the cabin condition\" [level=3]\n    - group \"Cabin condition\":\n      - button \"⚓ Stable cabin Predictable short crossings\"\n      - button \"🛰️ Station maneuver Changing reference + added drift\" [pressed]\n    - heading \"3. Choose how to move\" [level=3]\n    - strong: Carry a payload\n    - text: Same speed • more mass = more braking distance\n    - group \"Payload carried during translation\":\n      - button \"○ Hands free 0 kg • 1.00× inertia\" [pressed]\n      - button \"🧪 Specimen bag 4 kg • 1.15× inertia\"\n      - button \"🧰 Tool case 10 kg • 1.35× inertia\"\n    - strong: Outcome support\n    - text: See control predictions before moving.\n    - group \"Movement prediction mode\":\n      - button \"Guided\" [pressed]\n      - button \"Predict first\"\n    - region \"Current interior route\": Choose a different compartment to preview the route.\n    - group \"Microgravity movement method\":\n      - button \"Handrail travel Slowest • continuous contact Choose another compartment\" [disabled]\n      - button \"Gentle push + brake Coast, then counter-push Choose another compartment\" [disabled]\n      - button \"Hard push Fast • recovery likely Choose another compartment\" [disabled]\n    - group:\n      - text: 4. Work in the current compartment Hide setup\n      - paragraph:\n        - strong: \"Task:\"\n        - text: Tether the specimen bag before opening the experiment rack.\n      - paragraph:\n        - strong: \"Challenge:\"\n        - text: A loose sample keeps moving until a hand, rail, or wall stops it.\n      - text: 🛰️ Station maneuver Needs 2 control points\n      - group \"Work setup for Science lab\":\n        - button \"Body restraint + specimen tether ✓ Controlled Two control points • maneuver-ready Controlled setup predicted for maneuver conditions\"\n        - button \"One handrail + specimen tether ⚠ Recovery risk Lower control margin • stable cabin only Recovery likely during this maneuver\"\n      - paragraph: 1 work attempt in this compartment\n    - status:\n      - strong: Work recovery needed\n      - paragraph: During the maneuver, the rack force pulls your one-point brace off line and the specimen starts to drift. Re-brace at two points before retrying. The activity remains incomplete. Choose the maneuver-ready setup and retry.\n      - paragraph: Station maneuver • One handrail + specimen tether • recovery and retry\n    - button \"Reset practice\"\n  - text: 🧭 Commander's Hypothesis 20+ chars suggested\n  - paragraph: Before launch, predict what will matter most. Your debrief will compare this claim against the evidence you collect.\n  - button \"Use geology\"\n  - button \"Use astrobiology\"\n  - button \"Use atmospheric science\"\n  - textbox \"Mission hypothesis\":\n    - /placeholder: \"Example: I predict oxygen and hull margins will matter more than science points until we understand the radiation belts.\"\n  - text: 0/220 🎯 Optional Mission Objectives Bonus science available 🧪 Evidence chain +20 science\n  - paragraph: Connect observations to at least two dossier science goals.\n  - text: ⭐ Decision discipline +15 science\n  - paragraph: Make at least two optimal evidence-based decisions.\n  - text: 🛡️ Safe return margin +20 science\n  - paragraph: Finish with O2 and Hull both at or above 25%.\n  - paragraph: 👨‍🚀 YOUR CREW\n  - text: 🚀\n  - paragraph: Cmdr. Aisha Okonkwo\n  - paragraph: Commander\n  - paragraph: \"\\\"Stay calm, think clearly, act decisively.\\\"\"\n  - text: 🪨\n  - paragraph: Dr. Kenji Tanaka\n  - paragraph: Geologist\n  - paragraph: \"\\\"Every rock tells a story billions of years old.\\\"\"\n  - text: 🧬\n  - paragraph: Dr. Wei Chen\n  - paragraph: Biologist\n  - paragraph: \"\\\"If there's water, there might be life.\\\"\"\n  - text: 🔧\n  - paragraph: Eng. Marcus Johansson\n  - paragraph: Engineer\n  - paragraph: \"\\\"Redundancy isn't paranoia — it's survival.\\\"\"\n  - button \"← Back to destinations\"\n  - button \"🚀 Continue to power setup\"\n- status: Mission to Mars selected. Crew of 4 assembled. Review the briefing."}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@208"}
